        "date": "2026-11-14T19:52:11Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): Tormach lathe G76 J makes LinuxCNC's R1 ladder cut the record's passes\n\nLinuxCNC's G76 with R1 cuts J, 2J, ... clamped at K: ceil(K/J) passes.\ng76Grid floored J on its own, so the inch M12x2 thread posted J0.0314\nK0.0944 - four passes where the record laid and the verdict judged\nthree. J is now the shallower grid rounding while (n-1)J < K <= nJ holds\nfor the record's n rungs, else the one grid step up (never a full step\nover the record's first cut), else the record is refused by name.\nmm words are unchanged; the inch G76 golden's J is 0.0315.\n\nFixes #1619\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
